WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.670
Acting is a profession that requires a lot
of versatility and a willingness to test boundaries.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:11.990
Often, this bravery pays off with a critically
acclaimed performance that's lauded for years

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.260
or even becomes cinematic history.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.380
Sometimes, however, it results in a complete
nightmare for everyone involved.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.939
Ellen Page's bad joke

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.460
"Are you honestly and truly going to prom
with Katrina De Voort?"

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:27.660
"... Hi."

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.100
"Mia just said that you were gonna go with
her."

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.980
Juno was a critical darling upon its release
in 2007, but actress Ellen Page thinks the

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:42.110
indie comedy has one really big flaw... and
we're not talking about that hamburger phone

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.560
… or the overly stylized dialogue.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.440
"Silencio, old man…

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.500
Look, I just drank my weight in Sunny D, and
I gotta go pronto!"

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.280
The actress regrets Juno's joke about potentially
naming her baby "Madison."

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.300
"Isn't that, like, a little gay?"

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:05.100
Page told Bustle that the joke didn't register
with her at the time, but now that she's older,

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.080
she really wishes it hadn't happened.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.820
It's worth noting that Page came out as gay
in 2014, and she's become a vocal advocate

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.720
for LGBTQ rights.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:20.520
In fact, when Page performed a staged reading
of Juno for Planned Parenthood in 2017, she

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.740
skipped that line entirely.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.520
Denzel Washington is all wet

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:30.750
Based on the 1980s TV show of the same name,
The Equalizer stars Denzel Washington as Robert

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.510
McCall, a widower who works at a hardware
store when he's not busy killing bad guys.

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:41.070
In the film's climax, McCall lures some murderous
Russian gangsters to his place of employment…

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.560
where an explosion sets off the store's sprinkler
system.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:53.760
Looks boss, right?

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:59.700
Well, Washington told CinemaBlend he quickly
got real tired of being so damn wet.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:08.100
"By that third day, at about eleven at night,
after about a thireen hour day, I disagreed."

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.400
Still looks pretty boss, though.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.620
Margot Robbie gets messy

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.640
Actress Margot Robbie had a pretty bad time
making Suicide Squad.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.600
First of all, her character Harley Quinn wore
skimpy outfits that made her feel self-conscious.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.220
"You're welcome."

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:37.939
And she kept accidentally poking herself with
her spiky gold bangles.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.420
"Harley Quinn, nice to meet cha."

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:45.700
But when The Washington Post asked Robbie
what scene was her least favorite, she had

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.060
an answer at the ready.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:52.200
She absolutely hated filming that scene where
Quinn throws herself into a vat of white ooze.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:57.380
Robbie says she was utterly repulsed because
the nasty stuff kept getting into her ears

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.420
and nose.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:03.540
"I couldn't breathe, and I tried to open my
eyes, and it would glaze over my eyeballs,

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.989
and I could only see white.

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:05.680
It was horrible."

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.800
Chris Hemsworth: Shirts and skins

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.880
Actor Chris Hemsworth isn't too thrilled about
undressing on-screen these days.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.700
"Sorry I Tased you!"

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:22.060
He was perfectly fine being shirtless in the
first Thor film, but increasingly got annoyed

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:24.780
at those gratuitous scenes starring his abs.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:30.389
When Thor: The Dark World rolled around, director
Joss Whedon insisted he strip down after a

00:03:30.389 --> 00:03:31.420
big battle sequence.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:35.079
Speaking with MTV News, Hemsworth admitted
he was hesitant.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:36.980
"And he said, 'Chris, take your shirt off'...

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.520
And I said, 'Well, I don't know…

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.260
What's the why?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:41.840
What are we doing?"

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.260
The issue came up again during Thor: Ragnarok...

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.700
And the shirt came off again.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.120
Hemsworth told Access Hollywood he was relieved
he could keep his shirt on during the fifth

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:57.760
Thor film.

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:01.400
But director Taika Waititi felt the film needed
some eye-candy.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:05.860
"And then Tai came midway through shooting,
come up and said, 'I think we need to put

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:09.100
some bums on seats, I think we need to get
the shirt off,' and I was like, 'No, they

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:09.980
don't want to see that.'"

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.400
They did, though.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.380
Josh Brolin: God killer

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.150
It's fun playing the biggest bad guy in the
universe.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.180
Just ask Josh Brolin.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.100
He crushed it as Thanos in Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.600
And he reportedly really enjoyed tearing The
Hulk a new one.

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:49.520
But Brolin says he wasn't altogether pleased
about having to kill Loki.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.280
According to Brolin, actor Tom Hiddleston
was obsessed with getting Loki's last scene

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:03.060
just right, so filming became quite the bittersweet
bummer.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.610
Brolin told USA Today:

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.740
"Tom was so vulnerable at that moment.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.020
So choking him out wasn't the most fun thing
I have ever done."

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:14.980
Is it possible Loki will somehow be resurrected,
much like a certain Game of Thrones character

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:15.560
before him?

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:20.280
"Shhhh."

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.050
Kurt Russell's hateful fate

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.440
"I don't feel so good."

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:32.060
Directed by Quentin Tarantino, The Hateful
Eight was a lighting rod for hot takes and

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:33.140
angry opinions.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:38.250
But music lovers probably had the best reason
to hate the film... especially since Kurt

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.760
Russell destroyed a guitar that turned out
to be a priceless antique.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:47.660
"Music time's over."

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:50.020
"Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!"

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:56.100
Russell thought the guitar was a prop, but
it was actually an instrument from the 1860s…

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.220
and worth over $40,000.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.440
The incident really shook up Leigh, as she'd
fallen in love with the antique, and Russell

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:04.330
was devastated by what he'd done.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.840
"I'm already regretting this."

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:11.520
Speaking to Billboard, Leigh explained that
Russell "felt terrible" when he discovered

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:12.160
his mistake:

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.360
"When he found out, his eyes literally welled
up.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:19.840
It ended up being great for the scene, but
very sad for the guitar, and for my guitar

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:20.900
teacher, and for me."

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.220
Zoey Deutch's pizza problem

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.590
It's rare that a romantic comedy comes along
and breathes new life into the genre.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:33.780
But when Set It Up hit Netflix, critics were
delighted by the tale of two employees trying

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.080
to get their bosses to hook up.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:39.820
Starring Zoey Deutch and Glen Powell, the
film takes a predictable turn when the two

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:41.720
matchmakers fall in love themselves.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:46.700
In the film's most celebrated scene, the two
coworkers share a late-night pizza, which

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.150
sparks their romance.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:50.300
"This is the best meal I've ever had."

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:58.260
Unfortunately for Deutch, filming the scene
wasn't exactly romantic.

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:03.180
That's because she devoured four entire pies
while shooting that scene, and threw up halfway

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:04.190
through the shoot.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:08.360
And then she had to get very close to Glen
Powell in order to finish the shoot.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.500
She told Hello Giggles,

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:12.680
"I think [he] looks at me in a very different
light."

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:14.660
Fifty Shades of gross

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:19.810
Critics weren't the only ones who found Fifty
Shades of Grey alarmingly unsexy.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:25.620
Based on the runaway bestseller book of the
same name, the 2015 film stars Jamie Dornan

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:30.190
as the snooziest sadist ever … and Dakota
Johnson as his willing slave.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:34.820
"I need you to show me what you want to do
to me.

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:36.400
Punish me.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.760
Show me how bad it can be."

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:44.200
Unfortunately, filming all those bondage,
domination, and torture scenes could be pretty

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:44.720
bad.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:49.620
Johnson spent hours tied up, blindfolded,
and pretending to be struck by a whip.

00:07:49.639 --> 00:07:50.710
She told Time magazine,

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:53.460
"It's really hot—not in a steamy, sexual
way.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:56.360
It's just sweaty and it's not very comfortable."

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:00.760
She said the sex scenes were so taxing, she
started thinking, "Okay, let's just get this

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:01.260
over with."

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:06.460
Coincidentally, that's exactly what we were
thinking halfway through Fifty Shades of Grey.

